  <activity-date iso-date="2024-10-15" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Independent Researcher 1 will support Fight for Humanity&#x2019;s research efforts within the framework of the BCC Research Programme. Independent Researcher 1 is responsible for undertaking desk research, while following institutional policies and ethical standards.</narrative>
  </activity-date>
  <activity-date iso-date="2025-01-15" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner Organisation 3 will support Fight for Humanity&#x2019;s research efforts within the framework of the BCC Research Programme. Partner Organisation 3 is responsible for undertaking research, analysis of results, and producing research outputs, while following institutional policies and ethical standards. 

Partner Organisation 3 will work with the Fight for Humanity research team and coordinate with a small, international team of academics and practitioners to undertake research, analyse the results, and contribute to BCC research and policy outputs. 

Besides the contribution to the BCC research programme, Partner Organisation 3 may also be requested to contribute, based on the research conducted, as an expert source on the conflict context, providing analysis of trends and conflict dynamics related to harm and need, restraint and compliance in the Yemeni conflict.</narrative>
  </activity-date>
  <activity-date iso-date="2026-06-12" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner Organisation 4 will support Fight for Humanity&#x2019;s efforts within the framework of the BCC research programme. Partner Organisation 4 is responsible for disseminating research findings and contributing to the development of tools based on these findings.</narrative>
  </activity-date>
  <activity-date iso-date="2024-10-15" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner organisation 1 will support Fight for Humanity&apos;s research efforts within the framework of the BCC Research Programme. Partner organisation 1 is responsible for undertaking research, analysis of results, and producing research outputs, while following institutional policies and ethical standards. Partner organisation 1 will work with the Fight for Humanity research team and coordinate with a small, international team of academics and practitioners to undertake research, analyse the results and contribute to BCC research and policy outputs. Besides the contribution to the BCC research programme, Partner organisation 1 may also be requested to contribute, based on the research conducted, as an expert source on the conflict context, providing analysis of trends and conflict dynamics related to harm and need, restraint and compliance in the conflict.</narrative>
  </activity-date>
  <activity-date iso-date="2024-11-07" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner organisation 2 will support Fight for Humanity&#x2019;s research efforts within the framework of the BCC Research Programme. Partner organisation 2 is responsible for undertaking research, organising the data, and providing full interview data and an initial analysis of results, while following institutional policies and ethical standards.  

Partner organisation 2 will work with the Fight for Humanity research team and coordinate with a small, international team of academics and practitioners to undertake research, analyse the data and contribute to BCC research and policy outputs. Besides the contribution to the BCC research programme, partner organisation 2 may also be requested to contribute, based on the research conducted, as an expert source on the conflict context, providing analysis of trends and conflict dynamics related to harm and need, restraint and compliance in the conflict.</narrative>
  </activity-date>
